%S A402148 1,3,5,7,11,13,15,21,23,27,29,31,37,43,45,47,53,55,59,61,63,75,77,85,
%T A402148 87,91,93,95,101,107,109,111,117,119,123,125,127,149,151,155,157,165,
%U A402148 171,173,175,181,183,187,189,191,203,205,213,215,219,221,223,229
%N A402148 Numbers k such that the reversed k-th composition in standard order is a 1-based restricted growth sequence.
%C A402148 The k-th composition in standard order (graded reverse-lexicographic, A066099) is obtained by taking the set of positions of 1's in the reversed binary expansion of k, prepending 0, taking first differences, and reversing again. This gives a bijective correspondence between nonnegative integers and integer compositions.
%C A402148 A 1-based restricted growth sequence of length j is a sequence (a_1, ..., a_j), satisfying a_1 = 1 and a_i <= 1 + max(a_1, ..., a_{i-1}) for all i = 2, 3, ..., j.
%H A402148 <a href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0196885818300599">Campbell, Lindsey R., et al. "Restricted growth function patterns and statistics." Advances in Applied Mathematics 100 (2018): 1-42.</a>
%e A402148 The terms together with their standard composition begin:
%e A402148    1: (1)
%e A402148    3: (1,1)
%e A402148    5: (2,1)
%e A402148    7: (1,1,1)
%e A402148   11: (2,1,1)
%e A402148   13: (1,2,1)
%e A402148   15: (1,1,1,1)
%e A402148   21: (2,2,1)
%e A402148   23: (2,1,1,1)
%e A402148   27: (1,2,1,1)
%e A402148   29: (1,1,2,1)
%e A402148   31: (1,1,1,1,1)
%e A402148   37: (3,2,1)
%e A402148   43: (2,2,1,1)
%e A402148   45: (2,1,2,1)
%e A402148   47: (2,1,1,1,1)
%e A402148   53: (1,2,2,1)
%e A402148   55: (1,2,1,1,1)
%e A402148   59: (1,1,2,1,1)
%e A402148   61: (1,1,1,2,1)
%t A402148 stc[n_]:=Differences[Prepend[Join@@Position[Reverse[IntegerDigits[n,2]],1],0]]//Reverse;
%t A402148 rgoQ[y_]:=y[[1]]==1&&And@@Table[y[[i]] <= 1+Max@@Take[y,i-1],{i,2,Length[y]}];
%t A402148 Select[Range[100],rgoQ[Reverse[stc[#]]]&]
%Y A402148 For reversed partitions we have A055932, counted by A047967.
%Y A402148 Counted by A383253, triangle A383713, complement A402142.
%Y A402148 The non-reversed version is A402139, also counted by A383253.
%Y A402148 The non-reversed complement is A402141, counted by A402138.
%Y A402148 The normal complement is A402153 (non-reversed A402140, ranks A402143).
%Y A402148 A011782 counts compositions, strict A032020.
%Y A402148 A066099 lists compositions in standard order.
%Y A402148 A107429 counts normal compositions, ranked by A333217.
